<!--
    The Svartifoss mark: a musical note whose stem splits into the basalt columns the waterfall it
    is named after is known for.

    Traced from the brand asset (mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground) rather than redrawn, because a
    hand-approximated logo is a different logo. The trace is a straight-line contour of the source
    alpha at half-pixel tolerance - 0.1% of the ink differs from the original, on a mark that is
    then drawn at roughly a fifth of the traced size, so the polygons read as the curves they came
    from.

    A vector rather than a cropped bitmap so it can be tinted to whatever colour the text around it
    is using - see MusicGlyphs, which substitutes it for the note characters that turn up in lyric
    lines.
-->
